{"summary": "Wrote the explanation to /notebook/answer.txt.

Found the mechanism in module @tomlarkworthy/robocoop-5-srctools: the `applyLib` cell (`_190yjiu`, lines 352–623) exposes `applyModuleSrc`, which the file tools' write_file/edit_file/rc5_host paths all call. It compiles the edited /src source in-browser via `URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([src]))` + dynamic `import()`, then passes the module's `define(runtime, observer)` into `jbApply` (the notebook-kit 2.0 compile/decompile apply engine) to replace the module's variables in the live Observable runtime, so changed cells recompute and downstream cells react — reporting the compile status and per-cell error status back.

Answer written (one paragraph): a change to /src/<id>.js is applied by `applyModuleSrc` in `applyLib` of robocoop-5-srctools, which compiles the source in-browser and hands the resulting module define through `jbApply` into the live runtime, replacing the module's variables in place so cells recompute and downstream cells update."}

